# Opens Terminal with the FastSurfer console. build_release_package.sh compiles this into the
# FastSurfer applet with osacompile.
#
# `do script` runs this text in whatever shell Terminal is configured to start, which need not
# understand the setup script, so exec an explicit bash and give it the script as its init file.
# `exec` and `env` are spelled the same way in sh, bash, zsh, tcsh and fish, so this works from any
# of them. FASTSURFER_CONSOLE tells the script that ~/.bashrc has not been read;
# BASH_SILENCE_DEPRECATION_WARNING suppresses Apple's "zsh is the default now" notice, which is
# noise for a console that is bash on purpose. Both must be set before bash starts, hence `env`.
set console to "exec /usr/bin/env FASTSURFER_CONSOLE=1 BASH_SILENCE_DEPRECATION_WARNING=1 /bin/bash --init-file '/Applications/<fastsurfer>/macos_setup_fastsurfer.sh'"

if application "Terminal" is running then
	# a new window, so none of the user's open windows is taken over
	tell application "Terminal" to do script console
else
	# launching Terminal opens its first window by itself, so the console goes there rather than
	# into a second one. Waited for, but not forever: with no window after 5 s, open one.
	tell application "Terminal"
		activate
		repeat 50 times
			if (exists window 1) then exit repeat
			delay 0.1
		end repeat
		if (exists window 1) then
			do script console in window 1
		else
			do script console
		end if
	end tell
end if
tell application "Terminal" to activate
